cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DoX-Validate in a scientific publication, cite it as below and name EqualDoX as the developing organisation."
title: "DoX-Validate: PDF Accessibility Validator"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ehrhardt
    given-names: Matthis
    affiliation: EqualDoX
repository-code: "https://github.com/EqualDoX/DoX-Validate"
url: "https://github.com/EqualDoX/DoX-Validate"
license-url: "https://github.com/EqualDoX/DoX-Validate/blob/main/LICENSE"
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-11-13
abstract: >-
  DoX-Validate is a native command-line tool for automated PDF accessibility
  checks. It checks a PDF against PDF/UA-1, PDF/UA-2, WTPDF 1.0 and WCAG
  2.0/2.1/2.2 in a single pass, reports each machine-checkable violation with
  its page, object and rule, and lists the requirements that still need manual
  evaluation. Results are machine-readable (versioned JSON and JSON Lines).
keywords:
  - PDF
  - accessibility
  - PDF/UA
  - WCAG
  - WTPDF
  - validation
  - command-line tool
